'''Felyne''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] created by a collaboration event between [[Monster Hunter Collaboration Event|Battle Cats and Monster Hunter]]. It was added in [[Version 4.2 Update|Version 4.2]]. This unit can be unlocked by completing collaboration quests in the Monster Hunter Big Game Hunting Quest app.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 204
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Felyne
|name2 = Felyne & Melynx
}}

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
While Felyne's spammability and rapid attacks are great qualities for a crowd-controller, the rest of its kit massively works against it. Felyne's pathetic HP and range make it difficult to maintain a stack against nearly anything. Its targeted trait being [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] makes this even worse considering that Dark enemies are often spammed and thus require [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] to be properly stalled, and main threats like [[Shadow Boxer K]] and [[Gory Dark]] outrange Felyne and easily wipe it out. Even if [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] hasn't been acquired yet, [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Cat Gunslinger]] and even [[Tin Cat (Rare Cat)|Tin Cat]] are more worthy of use.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Felyne & Melynx go on to target a slightly more suitable trait. They just barely outrange [[Bore]] and [[One Horn]], but such enemies are still threats without primary crowd-control such as [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]] or [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]], and other Red enemies like [[Shy Boy]] outrange them. [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sushi Cat]] is by far a better choice against Red enemies, as they have Area Attack to apply Weaken to multiple enemies at once and impressive bulk to tank them—none of which Felyne & Melynx have.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Melee}}

